        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong class="text-white">Foundation Armor SX5000</strong> is a solid, well-documented silane-siloxane penetrating sealer that does exactly what that category promises: it soaks into the concrete, repels water and chloride from within, and changes nothing about how the slab looks.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          It is the right product for driveways, patios, and any exterior concrete where freeze-thaw and de-icing salt are the threats and appearance should stay as-is. It is the wrong product if you wanted gloss or a wet look. Confirm the slab is porous and genuinely dry, apply until it stops absorbing, and expect several years before reapplication.
